From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:45:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] http: add Chrome navigation keep-alive header

Emit Connection: keep-alive immediately after Host only on selected
HTTP/1.1 non-internal navigations, identified by the existing weight-256
classification. Apply an exact-match build-time overlay to pinned curl
http.c without editing dependency sources.

Preserve explicit Connection overrides and empty/suppression forms,
close/reuse restrictions, late TE and upgrade handling, HTTP/1.0, HTTP/2,
proxy CONNECT and non-navigation paths. Do not change TLS, compression
offers, client hints or the macOS persona.

Validation: ReleaseFast and Debug builds; 1658/1658 upstream tests;
22 temporary native-curl and browser diagnostics; all eight 20-sample
Chrome TLS scenarios. Recorder confirms the new header and position in
80/80 HTTP/1.1 observations, absence in 80/80 HTTP/2 observations, and
otherwise unchanged navigation header names, values and order across
all 160 observations. No new unit tests. Reviewer found no issues.

References: fingerprint/README.md and pinned curl 8.22.0 lib/http.c.
---
 build.zig                    | 116 ++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 tools/curl_http1_profile.zig |  55 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 122 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)
